 "note": "In-system freight for ships with no FTL drive. Every system has its main port plus a fuel depot, a moon base and a belt works (assumed, not yet on the world map). A hop between two sites costs delta-v and hours; fuel burned follows the rocket equation from the ship's mass, so heavy loads and long hops eat the tank. Pay is per tonne per km/s of delta-v, scaled by the difficulty level's local_pay_mult (solved with tests/solve_local.gd). The moon also has surface sites, the base's landing pad and a mining camp; they are only on the board for ships with lander legs that can land there (see landing.json), and runs that touch the surface pay surface_rate_mult more per tonne-km/s. Sol also has three outer stations (extra_sites): a cloud port at Venus, the Jovian works and the Saturn ring yards. Their hops are long (6 to 9.6 km/s), so they only show on the board for ships with the tanks to reach them.",
